cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use GPUCosmo, please cite the software as below. GPUCosmo is a research preview:
  please also state the version (or commit) used, and note that its independent full-likelihood
  validation is pending (docs/research_preview.rst). Please also cite the codes GPUCosmo is
  built on, for the parts you use: see "Citing" in README.md.
title: "GPUCosmo: GPU-native cosmological likelihoods and Bayesian evidence in JAX"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Medina-Varela
    given-names: Leonel
    affiliation: Carnegie Mellon University
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lhior/GPUCosmo"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.2.0
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - JAX
  - GPU
  - Bayesian evidence
  - Einstein-Boltzmann solver
  - likelihood
abstract: >-
  GPUCosmo evaluates cosmological likelihoods on GPUs with JAX: an emulator-free
  Einstein-Boltzmann solver for the CMB and matter power spectra, DESI DR2 BAO, Planck,
  ACT DR6 lensing and supernova likelihoods configured by Cobaya yamls, and a plug-in API for
  user likelihoods. Bayesian evidences for model comparison come from higher-order DALI
  expansions of the likelihood in the theory (third order by default, the order configurable,
  with a convergence check between orders) and tempered sequential Monte Carlo on them.
  Research preview.
